{
  "id": "2026-11-08-discoveryengine-v1alpha",
  "date": "2026-11-08",
  "api": "discoveryengine.v1alpha",
  "service": "Vertex AI Agent Builder",
  "title": "Discovery Engine: User Availability APIs & Breaking Changes",
  "summary": "Discovery Engine introduces new APIs for managing UserAvailability resources, including batch updates and listing. However, this update includes breaking changes: `name` and `parent` parameters are now strictly required in certain contexts, and `verification` and `updateTime` properties are now read-only.",
  "details": "Developers must update their code to accommodate several breaking changes. The `name` and `parent` parameters are now strictly required for certain methods; ensure these are always provided. Specifically, `name` for `checkFeaturePolicyMembers` and `parent` for `batchUpdate`, `list`, and `update` on `UserAvailabilities` are now mandatory. Additionally, the `verification` property in `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineFeaturePolicyMember` (and its alpha/beta variants) and the `updateTime` property in `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaUserAvailability` are now read-only. Any attempts to write to these fields will now fail.\n\nOn the feature front, new methods are available for `UserAvailability` resources: `projects.locations.userStores.userAvailabilities.batchUpdate`, `projects.locations.userStores.userAvailabilities.list`, and `projects.locations.userStores.userAvailability.update`. These enable programmatic management of user availability states. A new `projects.locations.collections.engines.checkFeaturePolicyMembers` method has also been added, allowing developers to pre-validate engine feature policy members against the project's directory before saving, helping prevent configuration errors.",
  "impact": "high",
  "breaking": true,
  "interesting_score": 9,
  "tags": [
    "breaking-change",
    "new-feature",
    "user-management",
    "access-control"
  ],
